## Distinct from a Class-2 statistical residual

A Class-2 statistical residual is the framework's "we know the
candidate set but cannot single one out; observation decides." A
structural closure is "we have single it out by substrate primitives;
observation is the consistency check." The K(t) leaf was *previously*
the former (per `era_timeline_disposition.md` Tier 3); this doc moves
it to the latter via the bridge in
`bicone_golden_z2_identification.md`.

The distinction matters because the empirical test now serves
*falsification* of the closure, not *selection* among candidates.
A measurement of `N_efolds ≈ 63.7` is **confirmation** of a forced
structural prediction; a measurement outside that band is a
**falsification** that requires going back to one of the closure
chain's steps and finding the failure.

